<problem>

<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" numToSelect="4" withReplacement="true" from="-10" to="10" />
  <selectFromSequence name="a" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" from="-10" to="10" />

  <select name="x" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false">p q r s u v w x y z</select>
  <math name="lhs" simplify="full">$a[1]*$x[1]+$b[1]*$x[2]+$b[2]</math>
  <math name="rhs" simplify="full">$a[2]*$x[1]+$b[3]*$x[2]+$b[4]</math>

  <math name="solution" simplify="full">(($b[3]-$b[1])*$x[2]+$b[4]-$b[2])/($a[1]-$a[2])</math>

  <math name="minus_byc" simplify="full">-$b[1]*$x[2]-$b[2]</math>
  <math name="minus_dx" simplify="full">-$a[2]*$x[1]</math>
  <math name="a_minus_d" simplify="full">$a[1]-$a[2]</math>
  <math name="rhs_2" simplify="full">($b[3]-$b[1])*$x[2]+$b[4]-$b[2]</math>
</setup>

<p>Solve for <m>$x[1]</m>.</p>
<md>
  <mrow>$lhs = $rhs</mrow>
</md>
<p><m>$x[1] =</m> <mathInput name="input1" /></p>
<answer>
<award referencesAreResponses="$input1"><when>
  $input1 = $solution
</when></award>
</answer>


<solution>
To solve for <m>$x[1]</m>, we move all terms involving <m>$x[1]</m> to the left side of the equation and move all other terms to the right side of the equation.  We add <m>$minus_dx</m> and then <m>$minus_byc</m> to both sides of the equation, obtaining
<me>$a_minus_d$x[1] = $rhs_2.</me>
Dividing by <m>$a_minus_d</m>, we obtain the solution
<me>$x[1] = $solution.</me>
</solution>

</problem>